{%- comment -%}
  "Chris Shi" as single-stroke cursive, for the signature intro on the
  portfolio index. Letterforms are the public-domain Hershey Script Simplex
  face (Allen V. Hershey, US NBS), laid out and smoothed by local/sig/sig_gen.py:
  each stroke is resampled at even arc-length, Gaussian-smoothed (endpoints
  fixed so strokes still connect), and fitted with Catmull-Rom, so the curves
  read as pen strokes rather than the font's integer-grid polylines. The
  underline flourish is hand-authored. Stroke order is writing order — the
  intro script draws each path in sequence by animating stroke-dashoffset.
{%- endcomment -%}
